/**
 * @addtogroup Foundation_BuildGuide_Precompiled 
 *
 * @section FoundationPrecompiledPurpose Purpose
 *
 * Precompiled libraries reduce build time for projects that consume Foundation.
 *
 * The repository remains the source of truth.
 * Users may build their own precompiled artifact depending on their target and
 * required feature macros.
 *
 * @section FoundationPrecompiledCompatibility Compatibility
 *
 * A precompiled library is only compatible with the toolchain, architecture,
 * ABI, and macro configuration used to build it.
 *
 * A Windows MSVC .lib is not assumed to be compatible with MinGW.
 * An ARM GCC Cortex-M3 soft-float .a is not assumed to be compatible with
 * Cortex-M4 hard-float.
 *
 * @section FoundationPrecompiledFullBuild Full Build
 *
 * A full build enables all Foundation modules.
 *
 * It is useful for:
 *
 * - desktop integration,
 * - testing,
 * - examples,
 * - quick prototyping.
 *
 * @section FoundationPrecompiledCustomBuild Custom Build
 *
 * A custom build enables only the required modules.
 *
 * It is useful for:
 *
 * - embedded systems,
 * - memory-sensitive projects,
 * - production firmware,
 * - target-specific deployments.
 *
 * @section FoundationPrecompiledRecommendedFlow Recommended Flow
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * cmake --preset <preset>
 * cmake --build --preset <preset>
 * cmake --install build/<preset> --prefix dist/<preset>
 * @endcode
 *
 * Or use:
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * ./scripts/export.ps1 <preset> <config>
 * @endcode
 */
